Termux uses desktop Linux build flags with Bionic. Preserve Chromium's Android
choice of ordinary mutexes even though BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) is false here.
pthread_mutexattr_setprotocol is unavailable at Termux's Android API 24 baseline.

--- a/third_party/zucchini/chromium/base/synchronization/lock_impl_posix.cc
+++ b/third_party/zucchini/chromium/base/synchronization/lock_impl_posix.cc
@@ -59,7 +59,8 @@
 // Lock::PriorityInheritanceAvailable still must be checked as the code may
 // compile but the underlying platform still may not correctly support priority
 // inheritance locks.
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_NACL) || BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA)
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_NACL) || BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA) || \
+    defined(__BIONIC__)
 #define PRIORITY_INHERITANCE_LOCKS_POSSIBLE() 0
 #else
 #define PRIORITY_INHERITANCE_LOCKS_POSSIBLE() 1
